<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Renaud de Dammartin</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1165–1227</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as Renaud I, Count of Dammartin</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Renaud de Dammartin was count of Dammartin and, through his marriage to Countess Ida in 1191, count of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boulogne-sur-mer">Boulogne</a>. Falling out with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philip-ii-of-france">Philip II of France</a>, he allied with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-king-of-england">King John</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a> and Emperor Otto IV and fought against Philip at Bouvines in 1214, where he was captured. He lost his lands and died in prison in 1227.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/renaud-de-dammartin.jpg" alt="Renaud de Dammartin" width="320" height="315" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Prisonniers_Bouvines.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
